  <diagram name="Design notes" id="notes">
    <mxGraphModel dx="3337" dy="1745" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="1600" background="#ffffff" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title_notes" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#334155;spacing=0;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;" value="Order and inventory design notes" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="1450" x="60" y="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_0" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Scope &amp; defaults&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;8 domain tables in schema inventory; Flyway history is technical, outside this count.&lt;br&gt;Multiple warehouses; one warehouse per order; whole-order fulfillment/cancellation only; integer quantities; PLN.&lt;br&gt;No categories, separate reservation table, partial fulfillment, transfers, expiry or post-fulfillment returns.&lt;br&gt;UUID IDs generated by the application; created_at defaults to now(); active defaults to true.&lt;br&gt;sales_orders.status defaults to DRAFT. stock_levels.on_hand/reserved default to 0; application sets updated_at." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="205" width="1500" x="60" y="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Keys &amp; checks&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;UNIQUE pairs: stock_levels(product_id, warehouse_id), order_items(order_id, product_id).&lt;br&gt;Other UQ fields are marked in the diagram. All fields NOT NULL except N; all FK use ON DELETE RESTRICT.&lt;br&gt;CHECK: on_hand &amp;gt;= 0; reserved &amp;gt;= 0; reserved &amp;lt;= on_hand; item quantity &amp;gt; 0; both unit prices &amp;gt;= 0.&lt;br&gt;role IN (ADMIN, OPERATOR); status IN (DRAFT, CONFIRMED, FULFILLED, CANCELLED).&lt;br&gt;IN: quantity_delta &amp;gt; 0 and order_id NULL. OUT: quantity_delta &amp;lt; 0 and order_id NOT NULL.&lt;br&gt;ADJUSTMENT: quantity_delta &amp;lt;&amp;gt; 0, order_id NULL, nonblank note required.&lt;br&gt;confirmed_at is NULL in DRAFT, required in CONFIRMED/FULFILLED, retained on cancellation.&lt;br&gt;Normalize user emails to lowercase; validate nonblank names/codes. Index FK not covered by existing PK/UQ indexes." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="286" width="1500" x="60" y="337" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Orders &amp; derived reservations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A DRAFT order may be empty. Confirmation requires at least one item and active products/warehouse.&lt;br&gt;Copy product_name, product_sku and unit_price into each item; quantity edits retain these snapshots.&lt;br&gt;UNIQUE(order_id, product_id): duplicate addition returns 409; update the existing item instead.&lt;br&gt;Confirmed items, customer and warehouse are immutable. Total = SUM(quantity * unit_price), not stored.&lt;br&gt;reserved = SUM(item.quantity) for CONFIRMED orders of the same product and warehouse.&lt;br&gt;No separate reservation lifecycle: this model assumes only whole-order confirmation, fulfillment and cancellation.&lt;br&gt;Deactivation does not prevent fulfillment/cancellation of already confirmed orders." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="259" width="1500" x="60" y="645" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_3" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;State transitions &amp; physical stock&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DRAFT → CONFIRMED: reserve all items (reserved + quantity); on_hand unchanged; no movement.&lt;br&gt;CONFIRMED → FULFILLED: on_hand − quantity, reserved − quantity; one OUT movement per item.&lt;br&gt;CONFIRMED → CANCELLED: reserved − quantity; on_hand unchanged; no movement.&lt;br&gt;DRAFT → CANCELLED: no stock effect. FULFILLED/CANCELLED are terminal; repeated invalid actions return 409.&lt;br&gt;IN and ADJUSTMENT change on_hand and append a movement; on_hand must remain at least reserved.&lt;br&gt;on_hand = SUM(quantity_delta) for the stock row. Start at 0 and add opening stock via IN.&lt;br&gt;Stock movements are append-only. OUT must match the linked order warehouse and one of its products." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="259" width="1500" x="60" y="926" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_4" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Transactions, locking &amp; missing rows&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For order mutations: lock sales_orders first, recheck status, then lock stock_levels in ascending id order.&lt;br&gt;DRAFT item/header edits also lock the order, preventing edits racing with confirmation.&lt;br&gt;Change status, counters and movement history in one transaction; failure of any item rolls everything back.&lt;br&gt;Receipts/adjustments lock stock_levels. A missing pair means zero availability.&lt;br&gt;First receipt: INSERT stock row ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, then lock/update it and append IN in one transaction.&lt;br&gt;Use PostgreSQL READ COMMITTED with explicit row locks; never read/check/write counters without synchronization.&lt;br&gt;Cross-table sums and OUT/order consistency are service invariants, verified by integration/concurrency tests." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="259" width="1500" x="60" y="1207" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_5" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Access &amp; verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ADMIN manages catalog, users and corrections; ADMIN/OPERATOR handle orders and receipts.&lt;br&gt;created_by/performed_by come from the authenticated employee, never an arbitrary request field.&lt;br&gt;Keep history; deactivate users/products/warehouses instead of deleting referenced rows.&lt;br&gt;Verify: overselling across orders; confirm/confirm, fulfill/cancel and edit/confirm on the same order; first-receipt race.&lt;br&gt;Diagram cardinalities describe FK constraints. Minimum one item at confirmation is an application rule." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="232" width="1500" x="60" y="1488" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
